{"title":"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4(calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4(calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Linear_Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Linear Algebra)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomial</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2dfc01ffddac6f0d55b378ad3aa0409042f2a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-x+x^2-x^3+\\cdots+x^{16}-x^{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" /> may be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812547792ae547f788dc3c71a7c7d840125c8e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0+a_1y+a_2y^2+\\cdots +a_{16}y^{16}+a_{17}y^{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"303\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe033362483e74682b80c748590496ee8b986201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />'s are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Constant\" title=\"Constant\">constants</a>. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_series\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Geometric series\">geometric series</a> formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cdfdee32d7958b92e0dd5570907510bb1f9ab4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - x + x^2 + \\cdots - x^{17} = \\frac {1 - x^{18}}{1 + x} = \\frac {1-x^{18}}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"338\" height=\"42\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c61b0ff84896892bfaafe847317398b3fc8035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef45d7080276598afae2d6353edd9e986ff13f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1-(y - 1)^{18}}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"102\" height=\"42\" />. We want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, which is the coefficient of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b70261cbbdbbe070d66a738ae05b44b41dbf1b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> term in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498955af5738e1c410ed9f80ab685d00763f37cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(y - 1)^{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"19\" /> (because the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in the denominator reduces the degrees in the numerator by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial_Theorem\" title=\"Binomial Theorem\">Binomial Theorem</a>, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c193b75c5439bc3460c0ec2b1fd1270bc9d17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1) \\cdot (-1)^{15}{18 \\choose 3} = \\boxed{816}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"211\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Again, notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c61b0ff84896892bfaafe847317398b3fc8035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. So\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610e73aabfb667ca1f5d67d2765f862d226494de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}1 - x + x^2 + \\cdots - x^{17} &amp; = 1 - (y - 1) + (y - 1)^2 - (y - 1)^3 + \\cdots - (y - 1)^{17} \\\\ &amp; = 1 + (1 - y) + (1 - y)^2 + (1 - y)^3 \\cdots + (1 - y)^{17}\\end{align*}.\" width=\"584\" height=\"79\" />\n</p><p>We want the coefficient of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a3faa3658bcbd8bde8e16cfa5baf019619fc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> term of each power of each binomial, which by the binomial theorem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81fad8ddfe63f1e7c9eb067f5648ab62ede21c12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2\\choose 2} + {3\\choose 2} + \\cdots + {17\\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"204\" height=\"53\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hockey_Stick_Identity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Hockey Stick Identity\">Hockey Stick Identity</a> tells us that this quantity is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e216c407573802cdabc454be7637da330a4c5528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${18\\choose 3} = \\boxed{816}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"109\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Again, notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/187903ac83b055fef8bc2c3c4464cdf07ab79d6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851018537a4268dffd3e893158af5b7d9f3aeb0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> gives: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610e73aabfb667ca1f5d67d2765f862d226494de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}1 - x + x^2 + \\cdots - x^{17} &amp; = 1 - (y - 1) + (y - 1)^2 - (y - 1)^3 + \\cdots - (y - 1)^{17} \\\\ &amp; = 1 + (1 - y) + (1 - y)^2 + (1 - y)^3 \\cdots + (1 - y)^{17}\\end{align*}.\" width=\"584\" height=\"79\" />\nFrom binomial theorem, the coefficient of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a3faa3658bcbd8bde8e16cfa5baf019619fc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4dbe2402da155165decf2cda36bbe84e2c373bdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2\\choose 0} + {3\\choose 1} + \\cdots + {17\\choose 15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"204\" height=\"53\" />. This is actually the sum of the first 16 triangular numbers, which evaluates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f6caf1901b3914234f02417708f1b8f42c03d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(16)(17)(18)}{6} = \\boxed{816}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"164\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4.28calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4(calculus)\">Solution 4(calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4(calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/708b1efda5790e7f4df3f590d1404cf02a9321a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=1-x+x^2-x^3+\\cdots+x^{16}-x^{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"317\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/6309436cc37d92dd92a83002e29ce4f380cd6478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(y)=a_0+a_1y+a_2y^2+\\cdots +a_{16}y^{16}+a_{17}y^{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"361\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Then, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/26056be265c65cbb1391e39ec7cdfc87838e2855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=g(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a606e855a66dcd0fca0b67b8be9446febf93ba3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{d^2f}{dx^2}=\\frac{d^2g}{dy^2}\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad1fdf559030b80d8ed800081b67d788a373531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d^2f}{dx^2} = 2\\cdot 1 - 3\\cdot 2x+\\cdots-17\\cdot 16x^{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"289\" height=\"39\" /> by the power rule.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f343423ac1350f26241fef742b78473d4a19953c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d^2g}{dy^2} = a_2(2\\cdot 1) + a_3(3\\cdot 2y)+\\cdots+a_{17}(17\\cdot 16y^{15})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"386\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Now, notice that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4c38a419ae56f13a202216dd45a1978bc91a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d5137b9d5ebad3a00086b0987fc4bd401ff214ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{&#39;&#39;}(-1) = g^{&#39;&#39;}(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc79787468264a3a728a51c85a9a8a95456bde90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{&#39;&#39;}(0)= 2a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"22\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/0812735b65529a56d08fffd8ea77424e7a925b26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{&#39;&#39;}(-1) = 2\\cdot 1 + 3\\cdot 2 +\\cdots + 16\\cdot 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"281\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can use the hockey stick theorem to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/3712dee985679f66f1348dc3f4329ecef7633972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 1 + 3\\cdot 2 +\\cdots + 16\\cdot 17 = 2\\binom{18}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"275\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f27c73dcbdd4916e74a9ea6be7f95be0392554.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a_2 = 2\\binom{18}{3}\\rightarrow a_2 = \\binom{18}{3}=\\boxed{816}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"285\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>-AOPS81619\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Linear_Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Linear_Algebra)\">Solution 5 (Linear Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Linear Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the vector space of polynomials of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88c594dd391254beae9ed76214498e44ba3b0f5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq 17,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a5b308b345365c1cb7a75096b9e11237f2f2cf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\{1, x, x^2, ..., x^{17} \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb858af6ac171ac9cf649a3ccec3692f68e9f55e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = \\{1, (x+1), (x+1)^2, ..., (x+1)^{17} \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"304\" height=\"21\" /> be two bases for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c0d207178faf2f2ca42af5098c9a93fdaced69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{v} \\in V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> be the polynomial given in the problem, and it is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/29023add3e9a3980e43c1f687d264c20823d89ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ \\vec{v} ]_B = \\langle 1, -1, 1, -1, ... , 1, -1 \\rangle.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Note that the transformation matrix from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> can be easily found to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a6b380bfefb08ad42ce09afdfb91dac3fffd06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{C \\to B} = [ [\\vec{c_1}]_B [\\vec{c_2}]_B ... [\\vec{c_3}]_B ] = \\begin{bmatrix} \\tbinom{0}{0} &amp; \\tbinom{1}{0} &amp; \\tbinom{2}{0} &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{0} \\\\ 0 &amp; \\tbinom{1}{1} &amp; \\tbinom{2}{1} &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{1} \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\tbinom{2}{2} &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{2} \\\\ \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\vdots \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{17} \\end{bmatrix} .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -57px\" width=\"453\" height=\"123\" />\n</p><p>I claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892636643b03db1f14fe211d2a7cea9110ef335b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{B \\to C} = \\begin{bmatrix} \\tbinom{0}{0} &amp; -\\tbinom{1}{0} &amp; \\tbinom{2}{0} &amp; \\cdots &amp; -\\tbinom{17}{0} \\\\ 0 &amp; \\tbinom{1}{1} &amp; -\\tbinom{2}{1} &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{1} \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\tbinom{2}{2} &amp; \\cdots &amp; -\\tbinom{17}{2} \\\\ \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\vdots \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{17} \\end{bmatrix} ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -57px\" width=\"336\" height=\"123\" /> where the term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de20972a352cbed526869ee609720e7d9a5aeb48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"35\" height=\"53\" /> is negated if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9ece7f97f556d5af63003cb94ecbc04def23999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> is odd. \n</p><p>One can prove that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th row of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/049a8244a53848ad4e188156ec2cf82f45e9200c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{C \\to B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> dotted with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />th column of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c25ec228c2d3e863a22ab0211c364566a6a9b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{B \\to C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6ab1a57ce73803c2940e7dc9e45d55c544c40dce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta_{i, j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"26\" height=\"19\" /> by using combinatorial identities, which is left as an exercise for the reader. Thus, since the two matrices multiply to form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/8997be13b564fe875017a89f550e0c66743c53c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{I}_{18},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> we have proved that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3efd565d564c321ffc18018d5e627ff0c14a822e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{B \\to C} = \\begin{bmatrix} \\tbinom{0}{0} &amp; -\\tbinom{1}{0} &amp; \\tbinom{2}{0} &amp; \\cdots &amp; -\\tbinom{17}{0} \\\\ 0 &amp; \\tbinom{1}{1} &amp; -\\tbinom{2}{1} &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{1} \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\tbinom{2}{2} &amp; \\cdots &amp; -\\tbinom{17}{2} \\\\ \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\vdots \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{17} \\end{bmatrix} .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -57px\" width=\"336\" height=\"123\" />\n</p><p>To find the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e25809cc8ec81373d3c46ff247a7c6d3a63dcaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{v}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> under basis <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737b15f20e17e7834a83b8188337bade510f22f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> we compute the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a6a87383abb3506a2ee7fd3425b7471415d9cb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ \\vec{v} ]_C = P_{B \\to C} [\\vec{v} ]_B = \\begin{bmatrix} \\tbinom{0}{0} &amp; -\\tbinom{1}{0} &amp; \\tbinom{2}{0} &amp; \\cdots &amp; -\\tbinom{17}{0} \\\\ 0 &amp; \\tbinom{1}{1} &amp; -\\tbinom{2}{1} &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{1} \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\tbinom{2}{2} &amp; \\cdots &amp; -\\tbinom{17}{2} \\\\ \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\vdots \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\tbinom{17}{17} \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} \\sum_{n=0}^{17} \\tbinom{n}{0} \\\\ -\\sum_{n=1}^{17} \\tbinom{n}{1} \\\\  \\sum_{n=2}^{17} \\tbinom{n}{2} \\\\ \\vdots \\\\  -\\sum_{n=17}^{17} \\tbinom{n}{17} \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} \\tbinom{18}{1} \\\\ - \\tbinom{18}{2} \\\\ \\tbinom{18}{3} \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ -\\tbinom{18}{18} \\end{bmatrix},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -60px\" width=\"712\" height=\"130\" /> where the last equality was obtained via Hockey Stick Identity.\n</p><p>Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2c93fc26150fef6bfd8d47b420175415548043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 =  [ [ \\vec{v} ]_C ]_3 = \\dbinom{18}{3} = \\boxed{816}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"230\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>-fidgetboss_4000\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME\" title=\"1986 AIME\">1986 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t